 "title": "Rainbows Are Full Circles",
 "cat": "physics",
 "emoji": "🌈",
 "sentences": [
  "Rainbows can actually appear as full circles.",
  "They form through refraction, reflection, and dispersion of light in water droplets.",
  "Sunlight creates these arcs opposite the sun, appearing in rain, mist, or spray.",
  "Primary rainbows show red on the outside and violet inside.",
  "Double rainbows feature a second arc with reversed colors.",
  "One observed rainbow lasted for 8 hours."
